Track 1: Orion's Lens Fractures
- Story & Context: Barnaby stood on the rooftop of the Osea station, pressing his telescope into the night sky until the metal grew cold enough to stick to his skin, suddenly hearing a digital screeching that synchronized perfectly with the rising tide beneath the floorboards. He knew then that the cables were transmitting the galaxy's own heartbeat, and the confusion left him trembling as he clutched a glass of bitter seawater. "The stars don't blink when the pressure breaks."
